Z||000007||Rodrv6||10-03-2000||03:59 PM||||Just turned 330,000 miles on the way home from work today on my 84. No, it's not the original engine, or transmission, or tie rod ends, or ball joints, or..............<BR>But it IS still a lot of fun <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||6
Z||000008||ur2biteme||10-04-2000||06:22 AM||||i just rolled over 170k on the original DIS duck about 4 days ago (need to update my signature)  i still have the original rack, tie rods(theyre shot though) lower ball joints were replaced a little while back though.  this engine is probably good for about 250-300k with good mantinence considering that i ran a compression check at around 140k and was getting consistent 150 psi readings on all cylinders (high was 151, low was 143) no knocks, rattles (other than the cat converter), smoke (other than my leaky valve cover gasket spilling oil into my spark plug holes) or anything like that.  i can only wish that i could say it had the original tranny.  lost that at 128k when my clutch decided to take the tranny with it!  i had thoughts of getting rid of this one, but decided against it.  boy am i glad!  (knocks on wood)<P>sorry for the bandwidth   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>169k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000009||DjKid||10-04-2000||06:46 AM||||My baby is sitting in the driveway with 133k on it.. not the original motor.. the motor has around 100k on it though.. still running cool..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> just needs a new motor mount.. seeing as how now it has none at all <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
